      "writtenOn": "2020-03-18T21:27:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The disconnecting pull types are from the spec, SNK-\u003eDRP is Rd/Rd and SRC-\u003eDRP is Rp/Rp\n\nYes, we want to set Rp/Rp for SRC-\u003eDRP. My question is: after tcpm_set_connection(port, TYPEC_CC_RP, 0) sets Rp/Rp, then we do set_state_tc(port, TC_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE) which will call tcpci_tcpc_drp_toggle() which will do tcpci_set_role_ctrl(port, 1, TYPEC_RP_USB, TYPEC_CC_RD), so it will change from Rp/Rp to Rd/Rd, which I don\u0027t think we want?",
      "parentUuid": "317a60dc_f994cda1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1704,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1704,
        "endChar": 21
